concatenation = 1\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 \fs20\lang1033\f0 The configuration file is a list of variables used by the Alligata Server, divided into groups. Each group controls a different area of the Alligata Server's functionality. The configuration file is a plain text file, so you can edit it in any text editor.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 When editing the configuration file, note the following points:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16\lang1024 \'95\tab \fs20 Groups must be separated by one or more blank lines.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16 \'95\tab \fs20 Each group must begin with the line\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260 \b\fs18\lang1033\f2  group = \i\fs16 identifier\i0\fs18  \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260 \b0\fs20\f0 where \i\fs18\f2 identifier\i0\fs20\f0  is one of the group identifiers listed in Figure 9.2.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16\lang1024 \'95\tab \fs20 The format of each variable definition is\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260 \b\fs18\lang1033\f2  \i\fs16 variable_name\i0\fs18  = \i\fs16 value\i0\fs18  \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260 \b0\fs20\f0 Quotation marks around the value are optional. Therefore,\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260 \b\fs18\f2  log-file = /tmp/bearer.log \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260 \b0\fs20\f0 is equivalent to\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260 \b\fs18\f2  log-file = "/tmp/bearer.log" \hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260 \b0\fs20\f0 However, quotation marks are required if the value begins or ends with a space, or if it contains special characters.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260 Within quotation marks, standard C escape character syntax operates:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li1160\sl260 {\*\bkmkstart _1015}{\*\bkmkend _1015}\b\lang1024 Table 9-1. Escape characters\sa100\keepn\par\trowd\trleft1160 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\