\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 \fs20\lang1033\f0 Remember that your microbrowser does not see this data but a compressed version of it that is less easy for a human being to decipher, but quicker to transmit and using less of the client device's limited memory.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 The first two tags in the file are the XML validation tags:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2 <?xml version="1.0"?>\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
<!DOCTYPE wml PUBLIC "-//WAPFORUM//DTD WML 1.1//EN"\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
    "http://www.wapforum.org/DTD/wml_1.1.xml">\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 \fs20\lang1033\f0 As we saw earlier, every WML file needs to start with these tags, which specify which versions of XML and WML the file conforms to (see Section 11.4).\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 Next comes the deck-level \fs18\f2 <wml>\fs20\f0  tag. Following that is the first card in the deck:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2  <card id="logo" ontimer="#menu" title="Welcome to ACME"    \sa0\par\fi0\sb0
 newcontext="true">\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
  <timer value="30"/>\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
  <img alt="ACME corp" src="acmelogo.wbmp" align="middle"/>\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
 </card>\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl260 \fs20\lang1033\f0 This is the card containing the ACME logo. Because it is the first card in the deck, it is the one that appears by default when you load the file.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 Here is a description of the card item by item.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 First, you will see that the \fs18\f2 card\fs20\f0  element contains four attributes:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16\lang1024 \'95\tab \fs18\f2 id="logo"\fs20\f0  gives the card a name by which other cards or decks can refer to it.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16 \'95\tab \fs18\f2 ontimer="#menu"\fs20\f0  tells the microbrowser that when the timer contained in the card runs out, it should load the card \fs18\f2 menu\fs20\f0 . The timer is defined in the \fs18\f2 timer\fs20\f0  element.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16 \'95\tab \fs18\f2 title="Welcome to ACME"\fs20\f0  defines a title to appear at the top of the card in the microbrowser.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16 \'95\tab \fs18\f2 newcontext="true"\fs20\f0  instructs the microbrowser to reset its 'context' when the card is loaded. A microbrowser's context consists of information it holds in its memory about recent events. Specifically, \fs18\f2 newcontext="true"\fs20\f0  removes all WML variables, clears the microbrowser's navigation history, and resets other information in the microbrower to its default value. precisely what information this is depends on the microbrowser.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 \lang1033 The next element is \fs18\f2 timer\fs20\f0 . It has the attribute \fs18\f2 value="30"\fs20\f0 , which tells the microbrowser to wait about three seconds before performing the action specified in the card's \fs18\f2 ontimer\fs20\f0  attribute.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 Note that, because \fs18\f2 timer\fs20\f0  is an empty element - that is, one without a closing tag - its tag must end in a forward slash /.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 The remaining element in the card is \fs18\f2 img\fs20\f0 , with three attributes:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16\lang1024 \'95\tab \fs18\f2 alt="ACME corp"\fs20\f0  tells the microbrowser to display the text 'ACME corp' if it cannot load the image for any reason.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16 \'95\tab \fs18\f2 src="acmelogo.wbmp"\fs20\f0  tells the microbrowser that the image to be displayed is the file \fs18\f2 acmelogo.wbmp\fs20\f0 .\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li1160\sl260\fi-200 \tx1160 \fs16 \'95\tab \fs18\f2 align="middle"\fs20\f0  tells the microbrowser to centre the image vertically, in relation to the surrounding text.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 \fs18\lang1033\f2 img\fs20\f0 , like \fs18\f2 timer\fs20\f0 , is an empty element, so the tag needs a forward slash / at the end of it.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 Finally, the card ends with a \fs18\f2 </card>\fs20\f0  tag.\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb100\li960\sl260 The second card in the deck looks like this:\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb200\li960\sl234 \fs18\lang1024\f2  <card id="menu" name="menu" title="The ACME Menu">\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
  <do type="prev" label="ACME home">\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
   <prev/>\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
  </do>\sa0\par\fi0\sb0
