concatenation = 1\hyphpar0\par\sect\sectd\plain\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1440\margrsxn1440\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1920\headery0\footery0\pgndec\titlepg{\headerf\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa430\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {}\par}{\footerf\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa910\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {\i\fs20 \chpgn }\par}{\headerl\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa430\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {\i\fs20 Appendix A. Appendix: Troubleshooting Guide}\par}{\footerl\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa910\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {\i\fs20 \chpgn }\par}{\headerr\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa430\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {\i\fs20 Appendix A. Appendix: Troubleshooting Guide}\par}{\footerr\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa910\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {\i\fs20 \chpgn }\par}\pard\sb311\s1\sl539 {\*\bkmkstart _3265}{\*\bkmkend _3265}\b\fs41\f1 Appendix A. Appendix: Troubleshooting Guide\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb207\li960\sl260 \b0\fs20\lang1033\f0 If you encounter any problems while running the Alligata Server, in the first instance you should check the log files for information. By default, the log files are held in the directory \fs18\f2 /var/log/alligata\fs20\f0 . You can view the log files by using the UNIX \fs18\f2 less\fs20\f0  command (for example, \b\fs18\f2 less /var/log/alligata/bearerbox.log\b0\fs20\f0 ). To watch a log file update while the Alligata Server is running, press SHIFT+F from within \fs18\f2 less\fs20\f0 .\sa200\par\trowd\trleft960\trhdr \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Problem\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Possible Cause\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \b\fs20\f1 Solution \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The Bearer Box will not start.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The configuration file contains errors.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Read Section 9 for information on how to edit the configuration file. Note that when you first install the Alligata Server, it will not be connected to an SMSC or a GSM modem. Therefore, if the configuration file contains any SMS variables, the Alligata Server may not start. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The WAP Box will not start.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 There are errors in the WAP Box configuration group.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Read Section 9 for information on how to edit the configuration file.\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvmgf\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The SMS Box will not start.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Your computer is not connected to an SMSC or a GSM modem.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 If you are subscribed to an SMSC, check that you are correctly linked to it and that you have configured the SMS Box and SMSC configuration groups properly (see Section 9). If you are using a GSM modem, check that it is correctly connected to the computer and that the SMS Box and SMSC configuration groups are properly configured. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvmrg\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \intbl\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 There are errors in the SMS Box or SMSC configuration groups.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Read Section 9 for information on how to edit the configuration file.\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvmgf\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The Alligata Server example sites cannot be viewed from a WAP client device.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The example sites have not been installed.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Rerun the installation program and install the example sites. (You do not need to reintall the Alligata Server.) See Sections 4 and 5 for installation instructions.\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvmrg\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \intbl\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 There is no HTTP server running on the same computer as the example sites.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Start your Web server and ensure that the example sites are in the correct directory for the server to find them (for example, in Linux, Apache looked by default in the directory \fs18\f2 /home/httpd\fs20\f0 . See Section 12 for instructions on viewing the example sites). If you have not installed a Web server, you can install the Apache server by rerunning the Alligata Server installation program and selecting the 'Apache Web server' option. (You do not need to reinstall the whole of the Alligata Server.) See Sections 4 and 5 for installation instructions. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The message '[OK]' was displayed when each Alligata Server box was started, but the Alligata Server is not responding to any WAP or SMS requests. \sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The Alligata Server may have been forced to close down by an error.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Check the Alligata Server log files for information about whatever caused the program to close down.\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 When the Bearer Box was instructed to start, the message 'Could not connect to the port' was displayed.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The Bearer Box is already running.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb100\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20\lang1033 At the Linux command prompt, type\b\fs18\f2  ps -ef | grep box \hyphpar0\par\pard\intbl\sb100\li100\ri100\sl260 \b0\fs20\f0 This will output a list that includes all Alligata Server processes. If any of the processes are named 'bearerbox', then the Bearer Box is already running.\sa160\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvmgf\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Outgoing SMS messages are not being sent by the Bearer Box.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The connection to your SMSC or GSM modem is faulty.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Check the connection to your SMS Centre or GSM modem. Ensure that the SMS Box and SMSC groups in the configuration file are properly set up.\sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvmrg\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \intbl\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 An SMS Service group is misconfigured.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Check in the configuration file that the relevant SMS Service group is properly configured. A common problem is that the \fs18\f2 max-messages\fs20\f0  variable is set too loiw. If an outgoing message needs splitting into more messages than allowed by max-messages, not all the messages will be sent. \sa60\cell \row \trowd\trleft960 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx3760\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx6560\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw20\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw20\cellx9360 \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Over-the-air (OTA) SMS configuration messages are not reaching the target mobile phone.\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 The variable \fs18\f2 max-messages\fs20\f0  in the OTA configuration group is set too low in the configuration file. (OTA configuration messages are usually too long to fit in a single SMS message.)\sa60\cell \plain \pard\intbl\sb60\li100\ri100\sl260 \fs20 Set the variable \fs18\f2 max-messages\fs20\f0  in the OTA configuration group to a value of 2 or higher.\sa60\cell \row \pard\plain\sl-1\hyphpar0\par}
